      "writtenOn": "2024-05-28T10:43:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@rwt pointed out that this patch could be dropped in favor of aosp/3088226.\nI wasn\u0027t sure because `p_dev-\u003einternal_send_fd` would then be written by both the btif and main thread.\nHowever, https://linux.die.net/man/2/write mentions that write is atomic, so probably nothing bad would happen. So I\u0027ll drop this in the next iteration.",
      "revId": "c31309a5a144bde814f9950dba8d5cef57a914a7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "06b138b1_331aaea2",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1960535
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-28T10:48:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hang on, even though write is atomic, it\u0027s still possible for the btif thread which owns `internal_send_fd` to close it, then the main thread would not know it and could still accesses the fd and crash. Maybe we still need this after all?",
      "parentUuid": "79fe61f8_8df228d9",
      "revId": "c31309a5a144bde814f9950dba8d5cef57a914a7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1e51309_246698e9",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-31T20:39:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can protect access to the bta_hh_co internal message queue with a mutex. It can be a global mutex for all connection instances. It is unlikely for the multiple HID devices to be connected at the same time, so it should not impact the performance.",
      "parentUuid": "06b138b1_331aaea2",
      "revId": "c31309a5a144bde814f9950dba8d5cef57a914a7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a3059a94_48da7f0c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1960535
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-03T07:17:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I think mutex will work, but I wonder why it\u0027s a better approach than doing it like this? After all, the other feature reports are passed through btif, so this is consistent with the flow.\nIs it perhaps because passing it to btif introduces a layer of delay that we don\u0027t want with input reports?\n\n\u003e It is unlikely for the multiple HID devices to be connected at the same time, so it should not impact the performance\n\nI think the busiest case might be two gamepad connected and used at the same time.",
      "parentUuid": "e1e51309_246698e9",
      "revId": "c31309a5a144bde814f9950dba8d5cef57a914a7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c18b29b6_9092d908",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-03T15:12:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. Adds another layer, new BTA message. Additional delay would be minimal but the design seems a bit complicated.\n2. Reports have to be protected anyway because of produce/consumer nature. So routing through BTIF is unnecessary.\nIf you feel strongly about it, we can move ahead at this time with the current approach. This is not a blocker.",
      "parentUuid": "a3059a94_48da7f0c",
      "revId": "c31309a5a144bde814f9950dba8d5cef57a914a7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d57ba13b_02d9aa36",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1960535
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-04T04:05:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e the design seems a bit complicated.\n\nYes, while I agree the design is complicated, but it matches the behavior of similar flow (e.g. feature report), so it doesn\u0027t add much burden to maintain and to understand it.\nAdding a mutex, on the other hand, introduces a new mechanism, therefore I think is complicated to maintain.\n\n\u003e Reports have to be protected anyway because of produce/consumer nature. So routing through BTIF is unnecessary.\n\nDo you mean we eventually need the mutex?\nI think we shouldn\u0027t need the mutex if the uhid thread and the btif thread aren\u0027t accessing the same struct. It\u0027s best if we can just separate the access. Otherwise we need to put mutex in a lot of places which looks dirty.\nIf we do this, we will still need to make sure the main thread and btif thread aren\u0027t shooting at each other\u0027s feet, so it\u0027s still necessary to route the events to btif (or alternatively, never route anything to btif).\n\nwdyt?",
      "parentUuid": "c18b29b6_9092d908",
      "revId": "c31309a5a144bde814f9950dba8d5cef57a914a7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
